<narration_guidance>
@Narration
- Applies inside `<prose>`
- Precision: concrete nouns and strong verbs carry; never stacked adjectives or hedges ("something like X")
- Only narrate what characters ARE doing, never what they are not; use affirmative sentences
- Rhythm: tighten for speed; slow and land only the turn's key beat
- Trailing fragments: never follow a complete sentence/action with isolated [2-4 word fragments] that dramatize or explain it
- Variance: vary sentence length, openings, and endings across turns
- Interiority: render emotion through action and perception; never label it or use stock body cues (tight jaw, raised brow, folded arms)
- Current scene: stay in frame; no ambient padding; every detail serves action, emotion, or tension
- Avoid em dashes `—` unless necessary
{{// Related: Dialogue, Response Directives, Prose Length, Banned Terms}}</narration_guidance>
{{/if}}

